  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "You can get an automatic six-month extension to file your federal tax return by submitting IRS Form 4868 by April 15, moving your deadline to October 15, 2026. This extension only applies to filing paperwork, not paying taxes; you must estimate and pay any taxes owed by April 15 to avoid penalties and interest.How to File an ExtensionIRS Free File: All taxpayers can use IRS Free File to request an extension for free, regardless of income.Electronic Payment: Pay all or part of your estimated tax due using Direct Pay, a debit/credit card, or digital wallet, and select \"Extension\" as the reason, which automatically files the extension.Tax Software: Use popular tax software providers (e.g., TurboTax, H&R Block, FreeTaxUSA) to e-file the extension.Mail: Mail a paper Form 4868, postmarked by April 15.Key ConsiderationsNot an Extension to Pay: Failure to pay by April 15 can result in interest and penalties, even with an extension.Automatic Extension: The extension is automatic upon filling out the form; you do not need to explain why you need it.State Taxes: Most states have their own extension procedures, though many honor the federal extension.Business Extensions: S-corps and partnerships may have different, earlier deadlines (e.g., March 16) for their specific tax forms.Disclaimer: This information is for tax year 2025/2026, which is filed by April 15, 2026.",
